  "answer": "The Atlas Logistics pilot was highly successful, with every metric in the results table exceeding its target: WAU reached 87.5% (target >75%), query success 84.2% (>80%), citation accuracy 88.6% (>85%), onboarding reduced to 4.8 weeks (target 5.0 weeks), support escalations declined 18.4% (>15%), and average latency was 1.8 seconds (<2.0s) `[NL-020#NL-020-S04]`. Key lessons identified were that pre-ingestion document cleanup is crucial, permissions should remain simple, and frontline teams need mobile optimization `[NL-020#NL-020-S07]`. Friction points to resolve before scaling included ingestion queue delays causing duplicate uploads and citation errors, mobile usability/hardware constraints (small screens, gloves, Wi-Fi drops), and reporting gaps in InsightDash `[NL-020#NL-020-S06]`. The expansion recommendation `[NL-020#NL-020-S08]` directly addresses these lessons through a phased rollout: Phase 1 expands to 500 users in Q3 2026 with a $2,500 fee and training webinars; Phase 2 implements advanced OCR in August 2026 to ingest legacy scanned documents; Phase 3 transitions to the Enterprise Plan in Q4 2026 if user count exceeds 2,000 (including drivers) with a Teams integration for mobile workers; Phase 4 establishes API integration and automated query audits in Q1 2027 to maintain citation accuracy.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
